      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "y",
      "answerEn": "what (as part of ¿y si...?, ‘what if...?’)",
      "noteEn": "At the start of ¿y si...?, y helps introduce another possibility for someone to consider rather than simply joining two items with ‘and.’",
      "example": { "es": "¿Y si llueve?", "en": "What if it rains?" },
      "tags": ["word", "fixed expression", "possibility", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-si--fixed-y-si",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "si",
      "answerEn": "if (completing ¿y si...?, ‘what if...?’)",
      "noteEn": "Si has no accent when it introduces the possibility after y. Together, ¿y si...? asks someone to consider what might happen.",
      "example": { "es": "¿Y si esperamos?", "en": "What if we wait?" },
      "tags": ["word", "fixed expression", "possibility", "A2"]
    },
